-- title:
--   Eichler order of level N inside the centralising quaternion algebra
-- statement:
--   Fix primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \ne r$, and a positive integer $N$ that is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$; let $k_0$ be an algebraically closed field (in the bottom universe) in which $N \ne 0$. Let $a,b \in \mathbb{Q}$ be such that $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and, for every height-one prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, its completion at $w$ is a division algebra exactly when $w$ contains $r$ or $\bar r$; let $\Lambda$ be a maximal order in it (an order not properly contained in another order) and $A_0$ an object of `FakeEllipticCurve Λ N k₀`. Further data are assumed, summarised in four groups. (1) A scheme $A$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec} k_0$, a relative group law $L$ on $f$, and an order $O$ in a quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d]$ that is definite ($c<0$, $d<0$) and a division algebra exactly at the primes containing $r$, with $O$ maximal, acting through $\varepsilon : O \to \operatorname{End}(A)$ by morphisms over $f$ which are homomorphisms for $L$, send $1$ to the identity, are additive and satisfy $\varepsilon(xy) = \varepsilon(y)$ followed by $\varepsilon(x)$. (2) A bijection $e_N$ from $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^2$ onto the $N$-torsion of the geometric points of $f$ over the point $\operatorname{Spec} k_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} k_0$ given by the identity, additive for $L$, together with $\mu : O \to M_2(\mathbb{Z}/N)$ describing the action of $\varepsilon$ on $N$-torsion through $e_N$, with $\mu$ surjective and $\mu(x) = 0$ precisely when $x \in N\,O$. (3) An algebra map $j : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b] \to M_2(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$ carrying $\Lambda$ into $M_2(O)$, morphisms $p_1,p_2 : A_0.A \to A$ over $k_0$ exhibiting $A_0.A$ as the fibre product of $f$ with itself and compatible with the group laws, and an assignment $E$ sending a matrix $y$ with entries in $O$ to an endomorphism of $A_0.A$ over $A_0.f$ which acts on points through $p_1,p_2$ by the matrix $y$ applied via $\varepsilon$, such that the $\Lambda$-action of $A_0$ is $m \mapsto E(j(m))$, and such that $E$ is additive, multiplicative in the reversed order, sends $1$ to the identity and respects the group law. (4) Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ definite and a division algebra exactly at the primes containing $\bar r$, an injective algebra map $\tau : \mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1] \to M_2(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},c,d])$ whose image is exactly the centraliser of $j(\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b])$, and $R$ the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of those $x$ with all entries of $\tau(x)$ in $O$. Finally let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$ containing $r$. The conclusion asserts the existence of $\mathbb{Z}$-submodules $\Lambda', R'$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ with $\Lambda'$ a maximal order, $R'$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (that is, an intersection of two maximal orders in which its additive relative index in the first is $N$), $R' \le \Lambda'$, and three further properties: first, a unit $x$ of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ lies in `awayUnits R' v` — the intersection, over all height-one primes $w \ne v$, of the preimages under localisation at $w$ of the subgroup generated by the local unit box of $R'$ at $w$ — if and only if there are $K,K'$ with $r^K x \in R$ and $r^{K'} x^{-1} \in R$ such that both $E(\tau(r^K x))$ and $E(\tau(r^{K'} x^{-1}))$ satisfy `PreservesLevel A₀ A₀`, i.e. carry points of $A_0$ factoring through $A_0.\mathrm{lev}$ to points factoring through $A_0.\mathrm{lev}$; second, every $y \in R'$ admits a $K$ with $r^K y \in R$ and $E(\tau(r^K y))$ preserving the level in this sense; third, there is a further maximal order $\Lambda''$ with $\Lambda' \cap \Lambda'' = R'$ such that each element of $R$ has an $r$-power multiple in $\Lambda''$ and each element of $\Lambda''$ has an $r$-power multiple in $R$.
--
--   This is the order-theoretic output of the moduli-theoretic analysis of fake elliptic curves with product structure: the order in the definite quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a_1,b_1]$ centralising the $\Lambda$-action, cut down by the requirement of preserving the level-$N$ structure, is realised as an Eichler order of level $N$, identified with the centraliser order $R$ after inverting $r$ and equipped with the two maximal orders whose intersection it is. It is used in the construction of a fake elliptic curve over $k_0$ together with a full endomorphism dictionary, where the Eichler order and its away-from-$v$ unit group feed the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset graph description.
